From: François Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: reset a PMF non-AP MLD that returns as a legacy
 station

A non-AP MLD with a PMF association can authenticate again as a legacy
station from its MLD address, for example after it lost its keys.
handle_auth() then clears its ML information but keeps the state machine
of the protected association, and the partner link stations stay.

Once the SA Query of the association times out, handle_assoc() resets
the earlier association only for an MLD station, so the legacy request
reuses the ML state machine: M1 carries the MLD MAC Address KDE and an
M2 without it is refused, and the station cannot connect until the
earlier association expires.

Also reset the earlier association, as for an MLD station, for a
station of an AP MLD whose SA Query timed out. ap_sta_re_add() then
frees the partner link stations of the earlier association.

Based on JiaY-shi's "AP: clean up stale MLD links after SA Query
timeout", which is otherwise covered by patches 181 and 876.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/ap/ieee802_11.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -7825,7 +7825,11 @@ static void handle_assoc(struct hostapd_
 	 * and FILS keep keys of the authentication in the state machine, so
 	 * only Open System and SAE authentication are covered.
 	 */
-	if (hapd->conf->wpa && ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta) &&
+	if (hapd->conf->wpa &&
+	    (ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta) ||
+	     /* a non-AP MLD that comes back as a legacy station */
+	     (hapd->conf->mld_ap && (sta->flags & WLAN_STA_MFP) &&
+	      sta->sa_query_timed_out)) &&
 	    ((sta->flags & WLAN_STA_ASSOC) ||
 	     ((sta->flags & WLAN_STA_MFP) && sta->sa_query_timed_out)) &&
 	    FULL_AP_CLIENT_STATE_SUPP(hapd->iface->drv_flags) &&
